  "modern": "Of such sensations and feelings as are agreeable or disagreeable, we may remark, it's a little, yet that they differ much, not only in degree, but in kind and in dignity. Some belong to the animal part of our nature, and are common to us with the brutes: others belong to the rational and moral part. The first are more properly called sensations, the last feelings. The French word sentiment is common to both."
